# $heightForText(pText,pMultilineObjRef) -> height in px, 0 = could not measure
# Measures the minimum height for pText to be FULLY visible in pMultilineObjRef.
# Measured on an invisible COPY of the field in the same window instance — the
# copy inherits font, fieldstyle, borders and scrollbar, so it is the only
# honest measuring stick. The original is NEVER touched.
# The width comes from the original as it is NOW: if it changes, measure again.
# No cap — what of the result fits is the caller's decision.
# Condition: $firstvis=1 and $lastvis=len(pText) (both count CHARACTERS).
If isclear(pMultilineObjRef)
	Quit method 0 ## no reference
End If
Calculate textLen as len(pText)
If textLen=0
	Quit method 0 ## empty text has no minimum height
End If
Set reference windRef to pMultilineObjRef.$wind()
If isclear(windRef)
	Quit method 0 ## window instance not reachable
End If

# Copy into the window instance. Per help, $add(object) creates a copy of the
# passed object; it lands congruent on the original.
Do windRef.$objs.$add(pMultilineObjRef) Returns copyRef
If isclear(copyRef)
	Quit method 0 ## copy failed
End If
Do copyRef.$visible.$assign(kFalse) ## nobody should see it
# Free it: otherwise the inherited $edgefloat governs the geometry and $height
# cannot be set (kEFposnClient inflates the copy to full window size).
Do copyRef.$edgefloat.$assign(kEFnone)
Do copyRef.$width.$assign(pMultilineObjRef.$width) ## width as the original has it NOW

# Content via #S1 and $dataname, $calculated off: with $calculated=kTrue, $text is a CALCULATION
# and pText would be evaluated as a formula.
Do copyRef.$calculated.$assign(kFalse)

Do copyRef.$dataname.$assign('#S1')
# #S1 belongs to the user: the reversible block restores it on every exit. Keep the block tight,
# everything inside is reversed. Only the Calculate form is reversible, $assign is not.
Begin reversible block
	Calculate #S1 as pText
End reversible block

Do copyRef.$redraw(kTrue,kTrue) ## once in full: load the content
# Read-back check: can the height be set at all? If not, the copy is externally
# governed and any measuring loop would spin without effect.
Do copyRef.$height.$assign(100)
Calculate readBack as copyRef.$height
If readBack<>100
	Do windRef.$objs.$remove(copyRef)
	Quit method 0 ## height externally governed — not measurable
End If

# Estimate the start value: line height from the font engine.
# $linecount is only a rough seed here; the measurement corrects any error.
Calculate lineHeight as 0
Do FontOps.$wintextheight(copyRef.$font,copyRef.$fontsize,copyRef.$fontstyle,copyRef.$linehtextra) Returns lineHeight
If isnull(lineHeight)|lineHeight<=0
	Calculate lineHeight as 14 ## fallback; the measurement corrects it anyway
End If
Calculate tryHeight as (copyRef.$linecount+1)*lineHeight ## deliberately OVERestimated
If tryHeight<lineHeight
	Calculate tryHeight as lineHeight
End If
Do copyRef.$height.$assign(tryHeight)
Do copyRef.$redraw(kFalse,kTrue)

# Derive the direction from the condition — the algorithm goes both ways.
Calculate fits as copyRef.$firstvis=1&copyRef.$lastvis=textLen
Calculate guard as 0
If fits
	# already fits: shrink coarsely until it breaks (coarse step = one line height,
	# smaller steps would have no effect inside a plateau)
	While fits&tryHeight>lineHeight&guard<500
		Calculate tryHeight as tryHeight-lineHeight
		Do copyRef.$height.$assign(tryHeight)
		Do copyRef.$redraw(kFalse,kTrue)
		Calculate fits as copyRef.$firstvis=1&copyRef.$lastvis=textLen
		Calculate guard as guard+1
	End While
End If

# grow finely: the first hit is the minimum height
Calculate guard as 0
While not(fits)&guard<5000
	Calculate tryHeight as tryHeight+1
	Do copyRef.$height.$assign(tryHeight)
	Do copyRef.$redraw(kFalse,kTrue)
	Calculate readBack as copyRef.$height
	If readBack<>tryHeight
		Do windRef.$objs.$remove(copyRef)
		Quit method 0 ## height became externally governed on the way
	End If
	Calculate fits as copyRef.$firstvis=1&copyRef.$lastvis=textLen
	Calculate guard as guard+1
End While

Do windRef.$objs.$remove(copyRef) ## clean up, on every exit
If fits
	Quit method tryHeight
End If
Quit method 0 ## guard tripped, condition never met